+# [Claude 2026-09-02 04:55 MSK: `git describe` is provenance, not a precondition for training.
+# Upstream lets a CalledProcessError propagate, so this function is fatal wherever the source is
+# not a git checkout -- which is every DataSphere job, because the payload arrives as a tarball.
+# Reproduced 2026-09-02 on a local rad run: exit status 128 here, after both environments were
+# built and before the first step. The run's real provenance is the payload SHA-256, which the
+# native run manifest records; this only stops a missing checkout from being fatal.
+# PLATFORM-class by setup/apply_patches.py's taxonomy: nothing measured changes.]
+def _describe_checkout():
+    try:
